{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-89515" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $L{f(t)}$ for the piecewise function defined by \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t)={\\begin{aligned}0,\\, & t<1 \\\\ -7,\\, & 1\\le t\\le 3 \\\\ 0,\\, & t>3.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043349/state.json" "file_sha256" "47535c0e35239cee5045e789748ef4bfb0c1d1568fe7ee21564f0180489729e1"} {"question" "q-89515" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We apply the definition of the Laplace transform:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{f(t)} & =F(s)={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}f(t)\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the piecewise function \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t)={\\begin{aligned}0\\, & \\text{for}\\,\\,t<1 \\\\ -7\\, & \\text{for}\\,\\,1\\le t\\le 3 \\\\ 0\\, & \\text{for}\\,\\,t>3\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwe have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(s) & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}f(t)\\text{d}t={\\int }_{1}^{3}(-7){e}^{-st}\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe calculate this definite integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(s) & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}(-7){e}^{-st}\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\frac{7}{s}{e}^{-st}|}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{s}({e}^{-3s}-{e}^{-s})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the Laplace transform of $f(t)$ is\n\n$$\nL{f(t)}=\\frac{7}{s}({e}^{-3s}-{e}^{-s}).\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043349/state.json" "file_sha256" "47535c0e35239cee5045e789748ef4bfb0c1d1568fe7ee21564f0180489729e1"} {"question" "q-89515" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043349/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "38a573db021f3f51d0d35b8e4caa096fc71ae1708fb2662e6b4930159ab54ee6"} {"question" "q-89515" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043349/state.json" "file_sha256" "47535c0e35239cee5045e789748ef4bfb0c1d1568fe7ee21564f0180489729e1"} {"question" "q-89515" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "L{f(t)}=\\frac{1}{7}({e}^{3s}-{e}^{s})"] ["math" "L{f(t)}=\\frac{1}{s}(1-{e}^{7s})"] ["math" "L{f(t)}=\\frac{7}{s}({e}^{-3s}-{e}^{-s})"] ["math" "L{f(t)}={e}^{-3s}-{e}^{-s}"] ["math" "L{f(t)}={e}^{-7s}-1"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043349/state.json" "file_sha256" "47535c0e35239cee5045e789748ef4bfb0c1d1568fe7ee21564f0180489729e1"} {"question" "q-89515" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "L{f(t)}=\\frac{7}{s}({e}^{-3s}-{e}^{-s})"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043349/state.json" "file_sha256" "47535c0e35239cee5045e789748ef4bfb0c1d1568fe7ee21564f0180489729e1"} {"question" "q-340886" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Use the definition of Laplace transforms to calculate $F(s)=L{f(t)}$ for $s>0,$ where $f(t)=u(5-t)$ and $u$ is the unit step function.$\\,F(s)=L{f(t)}=$ {{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043349/state.json" "file_sha256" "47535c0e35239cee5045e789748ef4bfb0c1d1568fe7ee21564f0180489729e1"} {"question" "q-340886" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We apply the definition of the Laplace transform:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{f(t)} & =F(s)={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }f(t){e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRecall that the unit step function is defined as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u(t)={\\begin{aligned}0,\\, & t<0 \\\\ 1,\\, & t\\ge 0.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, for the piecewise function \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u(5-t)={\\begin{aligned}1,\\, & t\\le 5 \\\\ 0,\\, & t>5\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwe have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(s) & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }u(5-t){e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{5}1\\cdot {e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{5}^{\\infty }0\\cdot {e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{5}{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe compute this integral for $s>0$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(s) & ={\\int }_{0}^{5}{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={[-\\frac{{e}^{-st}}{s}]}_{0}^{5} \\\\  & =-\\frac{{e}^{-5s}}{s}+\\frac{1}{s} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{s}(1-{e}^{-5s})\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043349/state.json" "file_sha256" "47535c0e35239cee5045e789748ef4bfb0c1d1568fe7ee21564f0180489729e1"} {"question" "q-340886" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043349/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "38a573db021f3f51d0d35b8e4caa096fc71ae1708fb2662e6b4930159ab54ee6"} {"question" "q-340886" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043349/state.json" "file_sha256" "47535c0e35239cee5045e789748ef4bfb0c1d1568fe7ee21564f0180489729e1"} {"question" "q-340886" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{1}{s}(1+{e}^{-5s})"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{s}(1+{e}^{-5s})"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{s}(1-{e}^{-5s})"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{s}({e}^{-5s}-1)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043349/state.json" "file_sha256" "47535c0e35239cee5045e789748ef4bfb0c1d1568fe7ee21564f0180489729e1"} {"question" "q-340886" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{s}(1-{e}^{-5s})"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043349/state.json" "file_sha256" "47535c0e35239cee5045e789748ef4bfb0c1d1568fe7ee21564f0180489729e1"} {"question" "q-340932" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Use the definition of Laplace transforms to calculate $F(s)=L{f(t)},$ where $f(t)$ is given by \n\n$$\nf(t)={\\begin{aligned}-1,\\, & x\\le 4 \\\\ 1\\, & x>4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$\\,F(s)=L{f(t)}=$ {{field-1}},\nvalid for {{field-2}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043349/state.json" "file_sha256" "47535c0e35239cee5045e789748ef4bfb0c1d1568fe7ee21564f0180489729e1"} {"question" "q-340932" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We apply the definition of the Laplace transform:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{f(t)} & =F(s)={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }f(t){e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, for the piecewise function \n\n$$\nf(t)={\\begin{aligned}-1,\\, & x\\le 4 \\\\ 1\\, & x>4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwe have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(s) & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }f(t){e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}(-1)\\cdot {e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{4}^{\\infty }1\\cdot {e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{0}^{4}{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{4}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that the improper integral diverges if $s\\le 0.$\n\nFor $s>0,$ we calculate our Laplace transform as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(s) & =-{\\int }_{0}^{4}{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{4}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{s}{[{e}^{-st}]}_{0}^{4}+{\\int }_{4}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{-4s}}{s}-\\frac{1}{s}+{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{4}^{a}{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{-4s}}{s}-\\frac{1}{s}+{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{(-\\frac{{e}^{-st}}{s})|}_{4}^{a} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{-4s}}{s}-\\frac{1}{s}-\\frac{1}{s}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }({e}^{-sa}-{e}^{-4s}) \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{-4s}}{s}-\\frac{1}{s}-\\frac{1}{s}(0-{e}^{-4s}) \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{-4s}}{s}-\\frac{1}{s}+\\frac{{e}^{-4s}}{s} \\\\  & =\\frac{2{e}^{-4s}}{s}-\\frac{1}{s}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nvalid for $s>0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043349/state.json" "file_sha256" "47535c0e35239cee5045e789748ef4bfb0c1d1568fe7ee21564f0180489729e1"} {"question" "q-340932" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043349/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "38a573db021f3f51d0d35b8e4caa096fc71ae1708fb2662e6b4930159ab54ee6"} {"question" "q-340932" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043349/state.json" "file_sha256" "47535c0e35239cee5045e789748ef4bfb0c1d1568fe7ee21564f0180489729e1"} {"question" "q-340932" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{s}-\\frac{2{e}^{-4s}}{s}"] ["math" "\\frac{2{e}^{-4s}}{s}+\\frac{1}{s}"] ["math" "\\frac{2{e}^{-4s}}{s}-\\frac{1}{s}"] ["math" "\\frac{{e}^{-4s}}{s}+\\frac{2}{s}"] ["math" "\\frac{{e}^{-4s}}{s}-\\frac{2}{s}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043349/state.json" "file_sha256" "47535c0e35239cee5045e789748ef4bfb0c1d1568fe7ee21564f0180489729e1"} {"question" "q-340932" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{2{e}^{-4s}}{s}-\\frac{1}{s}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043349/state.json" "file_sha256" "47535c0e35239cee5045e789748ef4bfb0c1d1568fe7ee21564f0180489729e1"} {"question" "q-340932" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043349/state.json" "file_sha256" "47535c0e35239cee5045e789748ef4bfb0c1d1568fe7ee21564f0180489729e1"} {"question" "q-340932" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "s>0"] ["math" "s>4"] ["math" "s\\ge 0"] ["math" "s\\ge 4"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043349/state.json" "file_sha256" "47535c0e35239cee5045e789748ef4bfb0c1d1568fe7ee21564f0180489729e1"} {"question" "q-340932" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "s>0"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043349/state.json" "file_sha256" "47535c0e35239cee5045e789748ef4bfb0c1d1568fe7ee21564f0180489729e1"} {"question" "q-341398" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Use the definition of Laplace transforms to calculate $F(s)=L{f(t)}$ for $s>0,$ where $f(t)=u(8-t)$ and $u$ is the unit step function.$\\,F(s)=L{f(t)}=$ {{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043349/state.json" "file_sha256" "47535c0e35239cee5045e789748ef4bfb0c1d1568fe7ee21564f0180489729e1"} {"question" "q-341398" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We apply the definition of the Laplace transform:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{f(t)} & =F(s)={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }f(t){e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRecall that the unit step function is defined as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u(t)={\\begin{aligned}0,\\, & t<0 \\\\ 1,\\, & t\\ge 0.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, for the piecewise function \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u(8-t)={\\begin{aligned}1,\\, & t\\le 8 \\\\ 0,\\, & t>8\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwe have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(s) & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }u(8-t){e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{8}1\\cdot {e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{8}^{\\infty }0\\cdot {e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{8}{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe compute this integral for $s>0$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(s) & ={\\int }_{0}^{8}{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={[-\\frac{{e}^{-st}}{s}]}_{0}^{8} \\\\  & =-\\frac{{e}^{-8s}}{s}+\\frac{1}{s} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{s}(1-{e}^{-8s})\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043349/state.json" "file_sha256" "47535c0e35239cee5045e789748ef4bfb0c1d1568fe7ee21564f0180489729e1"} {"question" "q-341398" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043349/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "38a573db021f3f51d0d35b8e4caa096fc71ae1708fb2662e6b4930159ab54ee6"} {"question" "q-341398" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043349/state.json" "file_sha256" "47535c0e35239cee5045e789748ef4bfb0c1d1568fe7ee21564f0180489729e1"} {"question" "q-341398" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{1}{s}(1+{e}^{-8s})"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{s}(1+{e}^{-8s})"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{s}(1-{e}^{-8s})"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{s}({e}^{-8s}-1)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043349/state.json" "file_sha256" "47535c0e35239cee5045e789748ef4bfb0c1d1568fe7ee21564f0180489729e1"} {"question" "q-341398" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{s}(1-{e}^{-8s})"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043349/state.json" "file_sha256" "47535c0e35239cee5045e789748ef4bfb0c1d1568fe7ee21564f0180489729e1"} {"question" "q-341390" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Use the definition of Laplace transforms to calculate $F(s)=L{f(t)},$ where $f(t)=u(t-3)$ and $u$ is the unit step function.\n\n$F(s)=L{f(t)}=$\n{{field-1}},\nvalid for $s\\,$\n{{field-2}}{{field-3}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043349/state.json" "file_sha256" "47535c0e35239cee5045e789748ef4bfb0c1d1568fe7ee21564f0180489729e1"} {"question" "q-341390" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We apply the definition of the Laplace transform:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{f(t)} & =F(s)={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }f(t){e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRecall that the unit step function is defined as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u(t)={\\begin{aligned}0,\\, & t<0 \\\\ 1,\\, & t\\ge 0.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, for the piecewise function \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u(t-3)={\\begin{aligned}0,\\, & t<3 \\\\ 1,\\, & t\\ge 3\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwe have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(s) & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }u(t-3){e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}0\\cdot {e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{3}^{\\infty }1\\cdot {e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{3}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that this improper integral diverges if $s\\le 0.$\n\nFor $s>0,$ we calculate this integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(s) & ={\\int }_{3}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{3}^{a}{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{(-\\frac{{e}^{-st}}{s})|}_{3}^{a} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{s}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }({e}^{-sa}-{e}^{-3s}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{s}(0-{e}^{-3s}) \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{-3s}}{s}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the Laplace transform of $f(t)$ is\n\n$$\nL{f(t)}=\\frac{{e}^{-3s}}{s},\\,s>0.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043349/state.json" "file_sha256" "47535c0e35239cee5045e789748ef4bfb0c1d1568fe7ee21564f0180489729e1"} {"question" "q-341390" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043349/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "38a573db021f3f51d0d35b8e4caa096fc71ae1708fb2662e6b4930159ab54ee6"} {"question" "q-341390" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043349/state.json" "file_sha256" "47535c0e35239cee5045e789748ef4bfb0c1d1568fe7ee21564f0180489729e1"} {"question" "q-341390" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{e^{-3s}}{s}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043349/state.json" "file_sha256" "47535c0e35239cee5045e789748ef4bfb0c1d1568fe7ee21564f0180489729e1"} {"question" "q-341390" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043349/state.json" "file_sha256" "47535c0e35239cee5045e789748ef4bfb0c1d1568fe7ee21564f0180489729e1"} {"question" "q-341390" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math ">"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043349/state.json" "file_sha256" "47535c0e35239cee5045e789748ef4bfb0c1d1568fe7ee21564f0180489729e1"} {"question" "q-341390" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043349/state.json" "file_sha256" "47535c0e35239cee5045e789748ef4bfb0c1d1568fe7ee21564f0180489729e1"} {"question" "q-341390" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043349/state.json" "file_sha256" "47535c0e35239cee5045e789748ef4bfb0c1d1568fe7ee21564f0180489729e1"} {"question" "q-341465" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Use the definition of Laplace transforms to calculate $F(s)=L{f(t)},$ where $f(t)$ is given by \n\n$$\nf(t)={\\begin{aligned}{e}^{5t},\\, & t\\le 1 \\\\ 1\\, & t>1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$\\,F(s)=L{f(t)}=$ {{field-1}},\nvalid for {{field-2}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043349/state.json" "file_sha256" "47535c0e35239cee5045e789748ef4bfb0c1d1568fe7ee21564f0180489729e1"} {"question" "q-341465" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We apply the definition of the Laplace transform:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{f(t)} & =F(s)={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }f(t){e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, for the piecewise function \n\n$$\nf(t)={\\begin{aligned}{e}^{5t},\\, & t\\le 1 \\\\ 1\\, & t>1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwe have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(s) & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }f(t){e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{e}^{5t}\\cdot {e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }1\\cdot {e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{e}^{5t-st}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{e}^{(5-s)t}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that the improper integral diverges if $s\\le 0.$\n\nFor $s>0,$ we calculate our Laplace transform as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(s) & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{e}^{(5-s)t}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5-s}{[{e}^{(5-s)t}]}_{0}^{1}+{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{(5-s)}-1}{5-s}+{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{1}^{a}{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{(5-s)}-1}{5-s}+{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{(\\frac{-{e}^{-st}}{s})|}_{1}^{a} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{(5-s)}-1}{5-s}-\\frac{1}{s}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }({e}^{-as}-{e}^{-s}) \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{(5-s)}-1}{5-s}-\\frac{1}{s}\\cdot (0-{e}^{-s}) \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{(5-s)}-1}{5-s}+\\frac{{e}^{-s}}{s}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nvalid for $s>0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043349/state.json" "file_sha256" "47535c0e35239cee5045e789748ef4bfb0c1d1568fe7ee21564f0180489729e1"} {"question" "q-341465" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043349/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "38a573db021f3f51d0d35b8e4caa096fc71ae1708fb2662e6b4930159ab54ee6"} {"question" "q-341465" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043349/state.json" "file_sha256" "47535c0e35239cee5045e789748ef4bfb0c1d1568fe7ee21564f0180489729e1"} {"question" "q-341465" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{{e}^{(5-s)}-1}{5-s}+\\frac{{e}^{-s}}{s}"] ["math" "\\frac{{e}^{(5-s)}-1}{s-5}-\\frac{{e}^{-s}}{s}"] ["math" "\\frac{{e}^{(5-s)}}{s-5}+\\frac{{e}^{-s}}{s}"] ["math" "\\frac{{e}^{(s-5)}}{s-5}+\\frac{{e}^{-s}}{s}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043349/state.json" "file_sha256" "47535c0e35239cee5045e789748ef4bfb0c1d1568fe7ee21564f0180489729e1"} {"question" "q-341465" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{{e}^{(5-s)}-1}{5-s}+\\frac{{e}^{-s}}{s}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043349/state.json" "file_sha256" "47535c0e35239cee5045e789748ef4bfb0c1d1568fe7ee21564f0180489729e1"} {"question" "q-341465" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043349/state.json" "file_sha256" "47535c0e35239cee5045e789748ef4bfb0c1d1568fe7ee21564f0180489729e1"} {"question" "q-341465" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "s>0"] ["math" "s>1"] ["math" "s>5"] ["math" "s\\ge 0"] ["math" "s\\ge 1"] ["math" "s\\ge 5"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043349/state.json" "file_sha256" "47535c0e35239cee5045e789748ef4bfb0c1d1568fe7ee21564f0180489729e1"} {"question" "q-341465" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "s>0"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043349/state.json" "file_sha256" "47535c0e35239cee5045e789748ef4bfb0c1d1568fe7ee21564f0180489729e1"} {"question" "q-341464" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Use the definition of Laplace transforms to calculate $F(s)=L{f(t)},$ where $f(t)$ is given by \n\n$$\nf(t)={\\begin{aligned}{e}^{3t},\\, & t\\le 2 \\\\ 2\\, & t>2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$\\,F(s)=L{f(t)}=$ {{field-1}},\nvalid for {{field-2}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043349/state.json" "file_sha256" "47535c0e35239cee5045e789748ef4bfb0c1d1568fe7ee21564f0180489729e1"} {"question" "q-341464" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We apply the definition of the Laplace transform:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{f(t)} & =F(s)={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }f(t){e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, for the piecewise function \n\n$$\nf(t)={\\begin{aligned}{e}^{3t},\\, & t\\le 2 \\\\ 2\\, & t>2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwe have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(s) & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }f(t){e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{e}^{3t}\\cdot {e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{2}^{\\infty }2\\cdot {e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{e}^{3t-st}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{2}^{\\infty }2{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{e}^{(3-s)t}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{2}^{\\infty }2{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that the improper integral diverges if $s\\le 0.$\n\nFor $s>0,$ we calculate our Laplace transform as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(s) & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{e}^{(3-s)t}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{2}^{\\infty }2{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3-s}{[{e}^{(3-s)t}]}_{0}^{2}+{\\int }_{2}^{\\infty }2{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{2(3-s)}-1}{3-s}+{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{2}^{a}2{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{2(3-s)}-1}{3-s}+{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{(\\frac{-2{e}^{-st}}{s})|}_{2}^{a} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{2(3-s)}-1}{3-s}-\\frac{2}{s}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }({e}^{-as}-{e}^{-2s}) \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{2(3-s)}-1}{3-s}-\\frac{2}{s}\\cdot (0-{e}^{-2s}) \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{2(3-s)}-1}{3-s}+\\frac{2{e}^{-2s}}{s}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nvalid for $s>0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043349/state.json" "file_sha256" "47535c0e35239cee5045e789748ef4bfb0c1d1568fe7ee21564f0180489729e1"} {"question" "q-341464" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043349/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "38a573db021f3f51d0d35b8e4caa096fc71ae1708fb2662e6b4930159ab54ee6"} {"question" "q-341464" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043349/state.json" "file_sha256" "47535c0e35239cee5045e789748ef4bfb0c1d1568fe7ee21564f0180489729e1"} {"question" "q-341464" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{{e}^{2(3-s)}-1}{3-s}+\\frac{2{e}^{-2s}}{s}"] ["math" "\\frac{{e}^{2(3-s)}-1}{s-3}-\\frac{2{e}^{-2s}}{s}"] ["math" "\\frac{{e}^{2(3-s)}}{s-3}+\\frac{2{e}^{-2s}}{s}"] ["math" "\\frac{{e}^{2(s-3)}}{s-3}+\\frac{2{e}^{-2s}}{s}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043349/state.json" "file_sha256" "47535c0e35239cee5045e789748ef4bfb0c1d1568fe7ee21564f0180489729e1"} {"question" "q-341464" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{{e}^{2(3-s)}-1}{3-s}+\\frac{2{e}^{-2s}}{s}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043349/state.json" "file_sha256" "47535c0e35239cee5045e789748ef4bfb0c1d1568fe7ee21564f0180489729e1"} {"question" "q-341464" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043349/state.json" "file_sha256" "47535c0e35239cee5045e789748ef4bfb0c1d1568fe7ee21564f0180489729e1"} {"question" "q-341464" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "s>0"] ["math" "s>2"] ["math" "s>3"] ["math" "s\\ge 0"] ["math" "s\\ge 2"] ["math" "s\\ge 3"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043349/state.json" "file_sha256" "47535c0e35239cee5045e789748ef4bfb0c1d1568fe7ee21564f0180489729e1"} {"question" "q-341464" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "s>0"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043349/state.json" "file_sha256" "47535c0e35239cee5045e789748ef4bfb0c1d1568fe7ee21564f0180489729e1"} {"question" "q-341451" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Use the definition of Laplace transforms to calculate $F(s)=L{f(t)},$ where $f(t)$ is given by \n\n$$\nf(t)={\\begin{aligned}3,\\, & t\\le 5 \\\\ {e}^{3t}\\, & t>5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$\\,F(s)=L{f(t)}=$ {{field-1}},\nvalid for {{field-2}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043349/state.json" "file_sha256" "47535c0e35239cee5045e789748ef4bfb0c1d1568fe7ee21564f0180489729e1"} {"question" "q-341451" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We apply the definition of the Laplace transform:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{f(t)} & =F(s)={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }f(t){e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, for the piecewise function \n\n$$\nf(t)={\\begin{aligned}3,\\, & t\\le 5 \\\\ {e}^{3t}\\, & t>5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwe have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(s) & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }f(t){e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{5}3\\cdot {e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{5}^{\\infty }{e}^{3t}\\cdot {e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{5}3\\cdot {e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{5}^{\\infty }{e}^{3t-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{5}3{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{5}^{\\infty }{e}^{(3-s)t}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that the improper integral diverges if $s\\le 3.$\n\nFor $s>3,$ we calculate our Laplace transform as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(s) & ={\\int }_{0}^{5}3{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{5}^{\\infty }{e}^{(3-s)t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{s}{[{e}^{-st}]}_{0}^{5}+{\\int }_{5}^{\\infty }{e}^{(3-s)t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{s}-\\frac{3{e}^{-5s}}{s}+{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{5}^{a}{e}^{(3-s)t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{s}-\\frac{3{e}^{-5s}}{s}+{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{(\\frac{{e}^{(3-s)t}}{3-s})|}_{5}^{a} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{s}-\\frac{3{e}^{-5s}}{s}+\\frac{1}{3-s}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }({e}^{(3-s)a}-{e}^{5(3-s)}) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{s}-\\frac{3{e}^{-5s}}{s}+\\frac{1}{3-s}\\cdot (0-{e}^{5(3-s)}) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{s}-\\frac{3{e}^{-5s}}{s}+\\frac{{e}^{5(3-s)}}{s-3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nvalid for $s>3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043349/state.json" "file_sha256" "47535c0e35239cee5045e789748ef4bfb0c1d1568fe7ee21564f0180489729e1"} {"question" "q-341451" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043349/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "38a573db021f3f51d0d35b8e4caa096fc71ae1708fb2662e6b4930159ab54ee6"} {"question" "q-341451" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043349/state.json" "file_sha256" "47535c0e35239cee5045e789748ef4bfb0c1d1568fe7ee21564f0180489729e1"} {"question" "q-341451" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{3}{s}+\\frac{{e}^{-5s}}{s}+\\frac{{e}^{5(3-s)}}{s-3}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{s}-\\frac{3{e}^{-5s}}{s}+\\frac{{e}^{5(3-s)}}{s+3}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{s}-\\frac{3{e}^{-5s}}{s}+\\frac{{e}^{5(3-s)}}{s-3}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{s}-\\frac{3{e}^{-5s}}{s}+\\frac{{e}^{5(s-3)}}{s-3}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043349/state.json" "file_sha256" "47535c0e35239cee5045e789748ef4bfb0c1d1568fe7ee21564f0180489729e1"} {"question" "q-341451" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{3}{s}-\\frac{3{e}^{-5s}}{s}+\\frac{{e}^{5(3-s)}}{s-3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043349/state.json" "file_sha256" "47535c0e35239cee5045e789748ef4bfb0c1d1568fe7ee21564f0180489729e1"} {"question" "q-341451" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043349/state.json" "file_sha256" "47535c0e35239cee5045e789748ef4bfb0c1d1568fe7ee21564f0180489729e1"} {"question" "q-341451" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "s>0"] ["math" "s>3"] ["math" "s>5"] ["math" "s\\ge 0"] ["math" "s\\ge 3"] ["math" "s\\ge 5"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043349/state.json" "file_sha256" "47535c0e35239cee5045e789748ef4bfb0c1d1568fe7ee21564f0180489729e1"} {"question" "q-341451" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "s>3"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043349/state.json" "file_sha256" "47535c0e35239cee5045e789748ef4bfb0c1d1568fe7ee21564f0180489729e1"} {"question" "q-341466" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Use the definition of Laplace transforms to calculate $F(s)=L{f(t)},$ where $f(t)$ is given by \n\n$$\nf(t)={\\begin{aligned}{e}^{t},\\, & t\\le 4 \\\\ 2\\, & t>4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$\\,F(s)=L{f(t)}=$ {{field-1}},\nvalid for {{field-2}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043349/state.json" "file_sha256" "47535c0e35239cee5045e789748ef4bfb0c1d1568fe7ee21564f0180489729e1"} {"question" "q-341466" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We apply the definition of the Laplace transform:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{f(t)} & =F(s)={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }f(t){e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, for the piecewise function \n\n$$\nf(t)={\\begin{aligned}{e}^{t},\\, & t\\le 4 \\\\ 2\\, & t>4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwe have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(s) & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }f(t){e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}{e}^{t}\\cdot {e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{4}^{\\infty }2\\cdot {e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}{e}^{t-st}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{4}^{\\infty }2{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}{e}^{(1-s)t}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{4}^{\\infty }2{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that the improper integral diverges if $s\\le 0.$\n\nFor $s>0,$ we calculate our Laplace transform as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(s) & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}{e}^{(1-s)t}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{4}^{\\infty }2{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1-s}{[{e}^{(1-s)t}]}_{0}^{4}+{\\int }_{4}^{\\infty }2{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{4(1-s)}-1}{1-s}+{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{4}^{a}2{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{4(1-s)}-1}{1-s}+{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{(\\frac{-2{e}^{-st}}{s})|}_{4}^{a} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{4(1-s)}-1}{1-s}-\\frac{2}{s}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }({e}^{-as}-{e}^{-4s}) \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{4(1-s)}-1}{1-s}-\\frac{2}{s}\\cdot (0-{e}^{-4s}) \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{4(1-s)}-1}{1-s}+\\frac{2{e}^{-4s}}{s}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nvalid for $s>0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043349/state.json" "file_sha256" "47535c0e35239cee5045e789748ef4bfb0c1d1568fe7ee21564f0180489729e1"} {"question" "q-341466" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043349/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "38a573db021f3f51d0d35b8e4caa096fc71ae1708fb2662e6b4930159ab54ee6"} {"question" "q-341466" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043349/state.json" "file_sha256" "47535c0e35239cee5045e789748ef4bfb0c1d1568fe7ee21564f0180489729e1"} {"question" "q-341466" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{{e}^{4(1-s)}-1}{1-s}+\\frac{2{e}^{-4s}}{s}"] ["math" "\\frac{{e}^{4(1-s)}-1}{s-1}-\\frac{2{e}^{-4s}}{s}"] ["math" "\\frac{{e}^{4(1-s)}}{s-1}+\\frac{2{e}^{-4s}}{s}"] ["math" "\\frac{{e}^{4(s-1)}}{s-1}+\\frac{2{e}^{-4s}}{s}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043349/state.json" "file_sha256" "47535c0e35239cee5045e789748ef4bfb0c1d1568fe7ee21564f0180489729e1"} {"question" "q-341466" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{{e}^{4(1-s)}-1}{1-s}+\\frac{2{e}^{-4s}}{s}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043349/state.json" "file_sha256" "47535c0e35239cee5045e789748ef4bfb0c1d1568fe7ee21564f0180489729e1"} {"question" "q-341466" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043349/state.json" "file_sha256" "47535c0e35239cee5045e789748ef4bfb0c1d1568fe7ee21564f0180489729e1"} {"question" "q-341466" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "s>0"] ["math" "s>1"] ["math" "s>4"] ["math" "s\\ge 0"] ["math" "s\\ge 1"] ["math" "s\\ge 4"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043349/state.json" "file_sha256" "47535c0e35239cee5045e789748ef4bfb0c1d1568fe7ee21564f0180489729e1"} {"question" "q-341466" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "s>0"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043349/state.json" "file_sha256" "47535c0e35239cee5045e789748ef4bfb0c1d1568fe7ee21564f0180489729e1"} {"question" "q-341481" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Use the definition of Laplace transforms to calculate $F(s)=L{f(t)},$ where $f(t)$ is given by \n\n$$\nf(t)={\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-3t},\\, & t\\le 1 \\\\ 4\\, & t>1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$\\,F(s)=L{f(t)}=$ {{field-1}},\nvalid for {{field-2}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043349/state.json" "file_sha256" "47535c0e35239cee5045e789748ef4bfb0c1d1568fe7ee21564f0180489729e1"} {"question" "q-341481" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We apply the definition of the Laplace transform:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{f(t)} & =F(s)={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }f(t){e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, for the piecewise function \n\n$$\nf(t)={\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-3t},\\, & t\\le 1 \\\\ 4\\, & t>1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwe have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(s) & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }f(t){e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{e}^{-3t}\\cdot {e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }4\\cdot {e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{e}^{-3t-st}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }4\\cdot {e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{e}^{-(3+s)t}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }4{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that the improper integral diverges if $s\\le 0.$\n\nFor $s>0,$ we calculate our Laplace transform as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(s) & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{e}^{-(3+s)t}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }4{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{-(3+s)}{[{e}^{-(3+s)t}]}_{0}^{1}+{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }4{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{1-{e}^{-(3+s)}}{3+s}+{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{1}^{a}4{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{1-{e}^{-(3+s)}}{3+s}+{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{(\\frac{-4{e}^{-st}}{s})|}_{1}^{a} \\\\  & =\\frac{1-{e}^{-(3+s)}}{3+s}-\\frac{4}{s}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }({e}^{-as}-{e}^{-s}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1-{e}^{-(3+s)}}{3+s}-\\frac{4}{s}\\cdot (0-{e}^{-s}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1-{e}^{-(3+s)}}{3+s}+\\frac{4{e}^{-s}}{s}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nvalid for $s>0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043349/state.json" "file_sha256" "47535c0e35239cee5045e789748ef4bfb0c1d1568fe7ee21564f0180489729e1"} {"question" "q-341481" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043349/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "38a573db021f3f51d0d35b8e4caa096fc71ae1708fb2662e6b4930159ab54ee6"} {"question" "q-341481" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043349/state.json" "file_sha256" "47535c0e35239cee5045e789748ef4bfb0c1d1568fe7ee21564f0180489729e1"} {"question" "q-341481" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1-{e}^{-(3+s)}}{3+s}+\\frac{4{e}^{-s}}{s}"] ["math" "\\frac{{e}^{(3+s)}}{s+3}+\\frac{4{e}^{-s}}{s}"] ["math" "\\frac{{e}^{-(3+s)}-1}{s+3}-\\frac{4{e}^{-s}}{s}"] ["math" "\\frac{{e}^{-(3+s)}}{s+3}+\\frac{4{e}^{-s}}{s}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043349/state.json" "file_sha256" "47535c0e35239cee5045e789748ef4bfb0c1d1568fe7ee21564f0180489729e1"} {"question" "q-341481" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1-{e}^{-(3+s)}}{3+s}+\\frac{4{e}^{-s}}{s}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043349/state.json" "file_sha256" "47535c0e35239cee5045e789748ef4bfb0c1d1568fe7ee21564f0180489729e1"} {"question" "q-341481" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043349/state.json" "file_sha256" "47535c0e35239cee5045e789748ef4bfb0c1d1568fe7ee21564f0180489729e1"} {"question" "q-341481" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "s>-3"] ["math" "s>0"] ["math" "s>1"] ["math" "s\\ge -3"] ["math" "s\\ge 0"] ["math" "s\\ge 1"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043349/state.json" "file_sha256" "47535c0e35239cee5045e789748ef4bfb0c1d1568fe7ee21564f0180489729e1"} {"question" "q-341481" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "s>0"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043349/state.json" "file_sha256" "47535c0e35239cee5045e789748ef4bfb0c1d1568fe7ee21564f0180489729e1"} {"question" "e-6641" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Use the definition of Laplace transforms to calculate $F(s) = \\mathcal L\\{f(t)\\}$ for $f(t) = u(t - 2) + u(t-6),$ where $u$ is the unit step function." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043349/example-6641.json" "file_sha256" "cde72ac2dc3328af621f23738e0092e862dbf687529e13415b2e6978d04abfd0"} {"question" "e-6641" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We apply the definition of the Laplace transform:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{f(t)} & =F(s)={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }f(t){e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRecall that the unit step function is defined as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u(t)={\\begin{aligned}0,\\, & t<0 \\\\ 1,\\, & t\\ge 0.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, for the piecewise functions $u(t-2)$ and $u(t-6),$ we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u(t-2) & ={\\begin{aligned}0,\\, & t<2 \\\\ 1,\\, & t\\ge 2\\end{aligned} \\\\ u(t-6) & ={\\begin{aligned}0,\\, & t<6 \\\\ 1,\\, & t\\ge 6.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043349/assets/6ddb2983dec1f3221778a336bb6ef3cce3138476b67d64334ab6660184a79f95.png)\n\nSo, for our Laplace transform, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(s) & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }f(t){e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}0\\cdot {e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{2}^{6}1\\cdot {e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{6}^{\\infty }2\\cdot {e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{6}{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{6}^{\\infty }2{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that the second integral diverges for $s \\leq 0.$\n\nFor $s > 0,$ we calculate our Laplace transform as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(s) & ={\\int }_{2}^{6}{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{6}^{\\infty }2{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{6}{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t+2{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{6}^{a}{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={[-\\frac{{e}^{-st}}{s}]}_{2}^{6}+2{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{(-\\frac{{e}^{-st}}{s})|}_{6}^{a} \\\\  & =-\\frac{{e}^{-6s}}{s}+\\frac{{e}^{-2s}}{s}-\\frac{2}{s}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }({e}^{-sa}-{e}^{-6s}) \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{-2s}}{s}-\\frac{{e}^{-6s}}{s}-\\frac{2}{s}(0-{e}^{-6s}) \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{-2s}}{s}-\\frac{{e}^{-6s}}{s}+\\frac{2{e}^{-6s}}{s} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{-2s}}{s}+\\frac{{e}^{-6s}}{s}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the Laplace transform of $f(t)$ is\n\n$$\n\\mathcal{L}\\left\\{f(t)\\right\\} =\\dfrac{e^{-2s}}{s} +\\dfrac{e^{-6s}}{s}, \n\\qquad \ns > 0.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043349/example-6641.json" "file_sha256" "cde72ac2dc3328af621f23738e0092e862dbf687529e13415b2e6978d04abfd0"} {"question" "e-21842" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Use the definition of Laplace transforms to calculate $F(s) = \\mathcal L\\{f(t)\\},$ where $f(t)$ is given by \n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043349/assets/e70e54b6a70cebd480b86baf9d0e1d90bde0b3d9277c982d5d5e77218d0d2f5d.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043349/example-21842.json" "file_sha256" "1e2df7bf46666ea3ac1c90f49b088e955a2c4532bd2de298f576b9fe24e028d8"} {"question" "e-21842" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We apply the definition of the Laplace transform:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{f(t)} & =F(s)={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }f(t){e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, for the piecewise function \n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043349/assets/48965cee8a09df4f637b4d997fdb9c90673e69a90ea1320434f9b471a2fed280.png)\n\nwe have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(s) & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }f(t){e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{e}^{2t}\\cdot {e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{3}^{\\infty }1\\cdot {e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{e}^{2t-st}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{3}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{e}^{(2-s)t}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{3}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that the improper integral diverges if $s \\leq 0.$\n\nFor $s > 0,$ we calculate our Laplace transform as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(s) & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{e}^{(2-s)t}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{3}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2-s}{[{e}^{(2-s)t}]}_{0}^{3}+{\\int }_{3}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{3(2-s)}-1}{2-s}+{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{3}^{a}{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{3(2-s)}-1}{2-s}+{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{(\\frac{-{e}^{-st}}{s})|}_{3}^{a} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{3(2-s)}-1}{2-s}-\\frac{1}{s}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }({e}^{-as}-{e}^{-3s}) \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{3(2-s)}-1}{2-s}-\\frac{1}{s}\\cdot (0-{e}^{-3s}) \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{3(2-s)}-1}{2-s}+\\frac{{e}^{-3s}}{s}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nvalid for $s > 0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043349/example-21842.json" "file_sha256" "1e2df7bf46666ea3ac1c90f49b088e955a2c4532bd2de298f576b9fe24e028d8"}] "usage" {"e-6641" [] "e-21842" []} "basis" 2595 "retractions" [[17592186228904 :question/problem "Use the definition of Laplace transforms to calculate $F(s) = \\mathcal L\\{f(t)\\}$ for $f(t) = u(t - 2) + u(t-6)$, where $u$ is the unit step function."] [17592186228904 :question/worked-solution "We apply the definition of the Laplace transform:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nL{f(t)} &= F(s) = ∫_{0}^{∞}f(t)e^{-st}dt\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRecall that the unit step function is defined as\n\n$$\nu(t) = {0,\\begin{vmatrix}t < 0 \\\\ 1,\\end{vmatrix}t \\ge 0\n$$\n\nSo, for the piecewise functions $u(t-2)$ and $u(t-6)$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nu(t - 2) &= {0,\\begin{vmatrix}t < 2 \\\\ 1,\\end{vmatrix}t \\ge 2 \\\\\nu(t - 6) &= {0,\\begin{vmatrix}t < 6 \\\\ 1,\\end{vmatrix}t \\ge 6\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{0,\\begin{vmatrix}t < 2 \\\\ 1,\\end{vmatrix}2 \\le t < 6; 2, \\mid t \\ge 6\n$$\n\nSo, for our Laplace transform, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nF(s) &= ∫_{0}^{∞}f(t)e^{-st}dt \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{2}0 \\cdot e^{-st}dt + ∫_{2}^{6}1 \\cdot e^{-st}dt + ∫_{6}^{∞}2 \\cdot e^{-st}dt \\\\\n&= ∫_{2}^{6}e^{-st}dt + ∫_{6}^{∞}2e^{-st}dt\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that the second integral diverges for\n\n$$\ns \\leq 0\n$$\n\nFor $s > 0$, we calculate our Laplace transform as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nF(s) &= ∫_{2}^{6}e^{-st}dt + ∫_{6}^{∞}2e^{-st}dt \\\\\n&= ∫_{2}^{6}e^{-st}dt + 2lim_(a → ∞)∫_{6}^{a}e^{-st}dt \\\\\n&= [- \\frac{e^{-st}}{s}]_{2}^{6} + 2lim_(a → ∞)(-\\frac{e^{-st}}{s}) \\mid _{6}^{a} \\\\\n&=-\\frac{e^{-6s}}{s} + \\frac{e^{-2s}}{s} - \\frac{2}{s} \\cdot lim_(a → ∞)(e^{-sa} - e^{-6s}) \\\\\n&= \\frac{e^{-2s}}{s} - \\frac{e^{-6s}}{s} - \\frac{2}{s}(0 - e^{-6s}) \\\\\n&= \\frac{e^{-2s}}{s} - \\frac{e^{-6s}}{s} + \\frac{2e^{-6s}}{s} \\\\\n&= \\frac{e^{-2s}}{s} + \\frac{e^{-6s}}{s}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the Laplace transform of $f(t)$ is\n\n$$\n\\mathcal{L}\\left\\{f(t)\\right\\} =\\dfrac{e^{-2s}}{s} +\\dfrac{e^{-6s}}{s}, \\qquad s > 0\n$$"] [17592186228895 :question/problem "Use the definition of Laplace transforms to calculate $F(s) = \\mathcal L\\{f(t)\\}$, where $f(t)$ is given by\n${e^{2t},\\begin{vmatrix}t \\le 3 \\\\ 1\\end{vmatrix}t > 3$."] [17592186228895 :question/worked-solution "We apply the definition of the Laplace transform:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nL{f(t)} &= F(s) = ∫_{0}^{∞}f(t)e^{-st}dt\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, for the piecewise function\n\n$$\n{e^{2t},\\begin{vmatrix}t \\le 3 \\\\ 1\\end{vmatrix}t > 3\n$$\n\nwe have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nF(s) &= ∫_{0}^{∞}f(t)e^{-st}dt \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{3}e^{2t} \\cdot e^{-st}dt + ∫_{3}^{∞}1 \\cdot e^{-st}dt \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{3}e^{2t - st}dt + ∫_{3}^{∞}e^{-st}dt \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{3}e^{(2 - s)t}dt + ∫_{3}^{∞}e^{-st}dt\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that the improper integral diverges if\n\n$$\ns \\leq 0\n$$\n\nFor $s > 0$, we calculate our Laplace transform as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nF(s) &= ∫_{0}^{3}e^{(2 - s)t}dt + ∫_{3}^{∞}e^{-st}dt \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2 - s}[e^{(2 - s)t}]_{0}^{3} + ∫_{3}^{∞}e^{-st}dt \\\\\n&= (e^{3(2 - s)} - 1)/(2 - s) + lim_(a → ∞)∫_{3}^{a}e^{-st}dt \\\\\n&= (e^{3(2 - s)} - 1)/(2 - s) + lim_(a → ∞)(\\frac{-e^{-st}}{s}) \\mid _{3}^{a} \\\\\n&= (e^{3(2 - s)} - 1)/(2 - s) - \\frac{1}{s} \\cdot lim_(a → ∞)(e^{-as} - e^{-3s}) \\\\\n&= (e^{3(2 - s)} - 1)/(2 - s) - \\frac{1}{s} \\cdot (0 - e^{-3s}) \\\\\n&= (e^{3(2 - s)} - 1)/(2 - s) + \\frac{e^{-3s}}{s}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nvalid for $s > 0$."]] "immutable_answers" [] "immutable_fields" [] "no_history" []}
